@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    var today = DateTimeExtensions.PakistanToday().ToString("MMMM d, yyyy");
}
<div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px 80px;font-family:-apple-system,'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif;color:#0f2220;line-height:1.65">
    <h1 style="font-size:28px;font-weight:800;margin-bottom:4px">ScholarshipHive Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p style="color:#5c7a75;font-size:13.5px;margin-top:0">Last updated @today</p>

    <p>ScholarshipHive is an internal workforce attendance and reporting app used by our own employees. This
    page explains what information the app collects, why, and who can see it. It applies to both the mobile
    app and this web admin panel.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><b>Account details</b> — your name, username, department, and role.</li>
        <li><b>Location</b> — precise location, including in the background while the app isn't open, used
            only to confirm you're physically at an approved office location when you check in or out. This is
            the core of how attendance is verified, so it isn't optional while you're using the app for work.</li>
        <li><b>Wi-Fi network identifiers</b> — the network your device is connected to, used as a second check
            alongside location to confirm office presence.</li>
        <li><b>A device identifier</b> — a random ID generated when the app is installed (not tied to your
            phone's hardware), used to recognize your own device for security features like the password-reset
            request and shared-device handling.</li>
        <li><b>Attendance records</b> — check-in and check-out times, generated automatically as you arrive and
            leave.</li>
        <li><b>Shift reports</b> — whatever you enter into your daily report (call/lead counts, notes, and any
            files you choose to attach).</li>
        <li><b>Push notification token</b> — used to deliver notifications to your device (for example, a
            password-reset confirmation), issued by Firebase Cloud Messaging.</li>
        <li><b>Fingerprint/biometric unlock</b> — if you turn this on, your fingerprint is verified entirely by
            your phone's own operating system. We never receive, see, or store your biometric data — the app
            only receives a yes/no "unlocked" result from your device.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">How this information is used</h2>
    <p>Everything above is used strictly for workforce management: recording attendance accurately, letting your
    manager review shift reports, and operating account-security features like device-verified password resets.
    We do not use this data for advertising, and we do not sell or share it with any third party outside the
    organization.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">Who can see your data</h2>
    <p>Only Admins and Auditors within your own organization can view attendance records, reports, and location
    status — and only through their own authenticated login. Other employees cannot see your data.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Attendance and report records are kept for as long as your account exists, as part of standard employment
    recordkeeping. You can ask an admin to review or remove your account at any time.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">Security</h2>
    <p>Data is sent over encrypted (HTTPS) connections. Passwords are never stored in readable form. Your login
    session on your phone is kept in your device's own encrypted secure storage, not in a plain file.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">Your choices</h2>
    <p>Location and notification permissions can be changed at any time from your device's Settings app —
    though since location is how attendance is verified, turning it off will prevent check-in/check-out from
    working correctly while you're using the app for work.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:19px;margin-top:36px">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy or your data can be sent to
        <a href="mailto:gmghulamgmghulam@gmail.com">gmghulamgmghulam@gmail.com</a>.</p>
</div>
